local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2008-03-27T00:01:15Z","user":"Fvasconcellos","size":1589,"width":180,"height":225,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg/500px-44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":384,"thumbheight":480,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg/960px-44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg/500px-44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":384,"height":480,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg/960px-44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:44th_Medical_Command_SSI.svg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=3780878","sha1":"e28eb147395c9f3e48632ddbcc5e126f288ee517","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-03-27 00:01:15","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"44th Medical Command SSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"44th Medical Brigade|With insignia|PD US Army USAIOH|Valid SVG created with Inkscape:Emblems|US Army Command Shoulder Sleeve Insignia","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder_Sleeve_Insignia_(US_Army)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (US Army)\">Shoulder Sleeve Insignia</a> of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/44th_Medical_Command_(United_States)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:44th Medical Command (United States)\">44th Medical Command</a>\n<dl><dt>Description</dt>\n<dd><i>On a white shield within a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) white border 2 inches (5.08 cm) in width overall a four-pointed gold star (with longer vertical points) superimposed on a maroon four-pointed star (points saltirewise and all of equal length) between two maroon flanks.</i></dd>\n<dt>Symbolism</dt>\n<dd>Maroon and white are the colors used for the Army Medical Service. The gold star superimposed over the maroon star is symbolic of the unit’s mission of command and control over medical units. The four points of each taken together allude to the organization’s numerical designation.</dd>\n<dt>Background</dt>\n<dd>This insignia was originally approved for the 44th Medical Brigade on 5 Oct 1966. The shoulder sleeve insignia was redesignated for the 44th Medical Command on 6 August 2001.</dd></dl>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2008-03-26","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"Own work based on: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.tioh.hqda.pentagon.mil/MedVet/44th%20Medical%20Command.htm\">The United States Army Institute of Heraldry – 44th Medical Command</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Fvasconcellos\" title=\"User:Fvasconcellos\">Fvasconcellos</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<i>This image shows a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/flag\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:flag\">flag</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/coat_of_arms\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:coat of arms\">coat of arms</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/seal_(device)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:seal (device)\">seal</a> or some other official <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/insignia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:insignia\">insignia</a></b> produced by the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Institute_of_Heraldry\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:United States Army Institute of Heraldry\">United States Army Institute of Heraldry</a></b>.  It is in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:public domain\">public domain</a></b> but its use is restricted by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/USCODE-2010-title18/pdf/USCODE-2010-title18-partI-chap33-sec704.pdf\">Title 18, United States Code, Section 704</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/704\">[1]</a> and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/granule/CFR-2012-title32-vol3/CFR-2012-title32-vol3-part507/content-detail.html\">Code of Federal Regulations (32 CFR, Part 507)</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/cgi-bin/text-idx?mc=true&amp;node=pt32.3.507&amp;rgn=div5\">[2]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/32/part-507\">[3]</a>.  Permission to use these images in the USA for most commercial purposes must be obtained from The Institute of Heraldry prior to their use.</i>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"insignia","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/svg+xml"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1042225853,"parentid":1041858503,"timestamp":"2025-06-10T02:53:09Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|description={{En|{{W|Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (US Army)|Shoulder Sleeve Insignia}} of the {{W|44th Medical Command (United States)|44th Medical Command}}\n;Description\n:''On a white shield within a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) white border 2 inches (5.08 cm) in width overall a four-pointed gold star (with longer vertical points) superimposed on a maroon four-pointed star (points saltirewise and all of equal length) between two maroon flanks.''\n;Symbolism\n:Maroon and white are the colors used for the Army Medical Service. The gold star superimposed over the maroon star is symbolic of the unit’s mission of command and control over medical units. The four points of each taken together allude to the organization’s numerical designation.\n;Background\n:This insignia was originally approved for the 44th Medical Brigade on 5 Oct 1966. The shoulder sleeve insignia was redesignated for the 44th Medical Command on 6 August 2001.\n}}\n|date=2008-03-26\n|source={{Based}} [http://www.tioh.hqda.pentagon.mil/MedVet/44th%20Medical%20Command.htm The United States Army Institute of Heraldry – 44th Medical Command]\n|author={{U|Fvasconcellos}}\n|permission={{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n{{Insignia}}\n|other fields={{Igen|Inkscape|+|s=em}}\n}}\n\n[[Category:44th Medical Brigade]]\n[[Category:US Army Command Shoulder Sleeve Insignia|Medical 044]]"}}}]},{"pageid":3927477,"ns":6,"title":"File:XV CORPS SSI.gif","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2008-04-23T03:46:17Z","user":"File Upload Bot (Magnus Manske)","size":2751,"width":162,"height":160,"duration":0.01,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/XV_CORPS_SSI.gif?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=image